pocket-motion-only: the PSP GE, Vita GXM and GLES2 paths address textures by power-of-two sizes and upstream keeps TEX_MAX_DIM at 512 for them; the software rasteriser samples by width and height and needs neither. A pak carrying an image of another size is refused by upstream's core at upload.

0020 — images of any size: an IMG pak entry, or a texture a host uploads,
is any size from 1 to IMG_MAX_DIM (2048) per side, a power of two or not.
Sprite atlases, tilesets and stream planes keep TEX_MAX_DIM (512) and
powers of two, and so every footage tile does.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs`
  (regenerated): `IMG_MAX_DIM = 2048`, and TEX_MAX_DIM's comment says what
  it still bounds.
- `engine/core/src/lib.rs`: `upload_texture_flags` takes each side in
  1..=IMG_MAX_DIM. Every size it accepted before it still accepts, the
  same way; sampling was already by width and height (`tex_quad`,
  `tex_tri`, `sample_linear`).
- `framework/compiler/pak.ts`: `encodeImageEntry` takes each side in
  1..IMG_MAX_DIM and names the size when it refuses; the header comment.
- `framework/src/host.ts`: the `uploadTexture` doc comment.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`: a 3x5 texture uploads and draws texel by
  texel at 10x, 2048 is accepted and 2049 refused.
- `tests/image-dims.test.ts`: a 300x170 entry encodes with its header and
  payload exact; 2048 encodes, 2049 is refused.

2026-10-22, rebased onto 66caf4e5: `tests/image-dims.test.ts` is listed
in `tools/test.ts`, which main's `tests/test-suite.test.ts` requires of
every test file.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

